WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.268 line:92%
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I really appreciate you
making the time.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:07.440
So you have been an undocumented
person for 25 years.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:07.874 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And when you wrote your boo
that won the Pulitzer,

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
you said "Notes of
an Undocumented Citizen."

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.948
Why was it important for you
to have "citizen" in the title

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, actually, I ended u
winning the Pulitzer

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was a reporter
for "The Washington Post."

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not for the book,
but thank you.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:24.758
-And I feel like you were
overlooked for the book

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm gonna
make a big point of it

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
next time I talk to my frien
Bob Pulitzer.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've got to love America,
though.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
I ended winning
a part of a Pulitzer

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.667 line:92%
but I can't get a Green Card

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:39.072
So, there's no process for
undocumented immigrants like me,

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have lived here 26 years
next month

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
to actually legalize our statu
and follow a process.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
Actually, I was watching
the debate tonight.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I actually started thinkin
that, coming on the show,

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to actually
make an announcement.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.290 size:88% position:44%
I think after tonight,
I am deciding to run for

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
President of the United States
of America.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.895 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Alright, yeah. Why not?

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.896 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:06.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On behalf of all
the undocumented immigrant

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the country.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm totally kidding.
Totally kidding.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:12.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because the reality is,
undocumented immigrants like m

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:17.777
can't even vote for an election,
much less participate in one

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You showed up when you were
12 years old

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.548 size:84% position:42%
from the Philippines,
and you did not realize

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
until you were 16 and tried to
get a driver's license

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.086 line:92%
that you lacked documentation.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.387 line:92%
Is that how it worked out?

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.555 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, that was in 1997.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.224 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Only 13 states allow

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
undocumented immigrants
to drive.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.395 line:92%
So I found out when I was 16

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.729 size:75% position:38% line:92%
There was no Google.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.165 line:92%
It's not like I can Google this.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I'm Filipino.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:44.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
And whenever the media sai
anything about illegal people,

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.705 line:92%
it was always about Mexico

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.174 size:84% position:42%
By the way, if you see
an Asian-looking person

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a Latino name,
it means they're Filipino.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.413 line:92%
That's a little hint from me

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's 4 million of us
in America.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:58.051 size:81% position:41%
So, I thought I may be
the only non-Mexican

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
undocumented immigrant
in this country.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then thankfully I was a studen
in high school,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.858 line:92%
and my teacher, Mrs. Door, sai

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I asked too many
annoying questions

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I should do this thing
called journalism.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:13.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I found out that
when you become a journalist

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you get a byline.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.269 size:81% position:41%
So, like, your name is
on a piece of paper.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.804 line:92%
so I thought if I can't be her

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I don't have
the right papers,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.441 line:92%
what if my name is on the paper?

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.278
Like, this book actually has
a Library of Congress number

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.713 line:92%
Like, I don't have a Green Card,

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the book is documented
and I'm not.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's all right.
-But what is that about, right

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.822
Like, actually, for me, now that
immigration is, like,

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
the central topic
in this election,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.960
I think there's an opportunity
for us to really educate peopl

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.797 size:88% position:44%
about what the issue is,
and what really a lot of

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
the politicians and even peopl
in the mainstream media

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.768 line:92%
is not really talking about.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.003 line:92%
-What are they getting wrong

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.004 line:92%
When you read coverage about it,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you watch a debate
like tonight,

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.440
what do you feel like people are
getting wrong

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.209 size:84% position:42%
when they talk about
the immigration debate?

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the number-one thing is
the fact that there is --

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
The number-one question I ge
asked all the time is

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.717 line:92%
"Why can't you just get legal?

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.720
As if all I have to do is
flip a switch and poof,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm an American
stealing your welfare, right

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even tonight
during the debate,

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.695 size:84% position:42%
when they talked about
undocumented immigrants

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
and healthcare,
undocumented workers like me

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually contribute
billions of dollars

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.535 line:92%
in taxes and Social Security

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:26.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I have paid so much taxe
this past tax season,

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.807 line:92%
I should be a Republican.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:28.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:35.215
So, we pay into the system
that deports and detains us.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.382 line:92%
Like, so what is that about?

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the fact is,
in the media, even now,

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm really sorry
to say this,

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:43.856
even "The Washington Post" and
"The New York Times" still refer

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.857 line:92%
to people like me as illegal

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
So Define American has actuall
been at the forefront of

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.963 size:81% position:41%
actually challenging
how news organizations

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:53.066
and then how television show
portray immigrants like me

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Talk about Define American,
and when you started it,

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.271 size:88% position:44%
and obviously those were
a couple of the goals,

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
but how you go about trying to
get people to listen.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, to be honest,
I'm only one story, right?

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, if I counted all
the undocumented white peopl

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.547 line:92%
that I meet at Starbucks -

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's where
they would hang out.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:11.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's where
they would hang out.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they tell me
they're undocumented,

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:16.022
and usually we don't talk abou
undocumented white immigrant

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
or even undocumented black
immigrants

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.392 line:92%
from Africa or the Caribbean

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
The reality is
the fastest-growing

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.630 size:84% position:42%
undocumented population
are coming from Asia,

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.364 size:84% position:42% line:92%
not from Latin America.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:28.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually think owe
the Mexican people an apolog

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.702 line:92%
for having made this issue

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:33.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
just about Mexican people
and just about Latin America

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
[ Applause ]

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:39.012
What? There's like 56 millio
Latin people in this country

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:39.946 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And the majority of them

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:43.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
have been here for decades
if not centuries.

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:43.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like, I don't know,

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:46.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
when California used to be
part of Mexico.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:49.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, to me, really, our goal is
how do we get people

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:52.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get this issue
out of this border Mexican box

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.426 line:92%
that we have locked it in.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.395 size:88% position:44%
And for us, storytelling
is the way to do that.

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:58.865
So if you're undocumented an
you want to share your story

00:04:58.865 --> 00:04:59.599 size:84% position:42% line:92%
if you're white, black,

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.834 size:81% position:41%
if you're an engineer
or if you're a farmer,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.170 size:75% position:38%
go to our website --
defineamerican.com

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:04.871 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and tell us your story

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
and help us get this issue
out of this box

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.374 line:92%
that we have relegated it in

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm so glad
you're doing that.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for making the time tonight.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:13.479 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it's just great

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.049
